# Keeping the build context small is the cheapest build-speed win there is: everything
# listed here would otherwise be shipped to the daemon on every single build, and any
# change to it would bust the layer cache.

# Build output — the image builds from source inside the SDK stage
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/
artifacts/

# Secrets must never enter an image layer, where they persist even if a later layer
# deletes them.
.env
.env.local
secrets.json
*.pfx
*.key
*.pem

# Version control and CI
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.gitattributes

# IDE
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo

# Test artefacts
**/TestResults/
coverage/
*.trx

# Runtime configuration mounted at run time, not baked in
docker/
docker-compose*.yml

# Documentation — irrelevant to the build, and README churn should not invalidate layers
docs/
*.md
!README.md
LICENSE
**/*.http

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
